# NOTE (spec item 9.1 - "reputation link is broken", superseded 2026-08-15):
# The original fix here was a wildcard SPA fallback (`/* /index.html 200`)
# so cold/deep-link requests like /reputation/<token>, /verify/:paymentId,
# and /onboard/:token would reach index.html/React Router instead of the
# host's default (which landed on /login).
#
# That rule now conflicts with wrangler.jsonc's
# `assets.not_found_handling: "single-page-application"`, which does the
# exact same job natively at the Workers-assets layer. Having both made
# Cloudflare's deploy-time loop checker see `/* -> /index.html -> (falls
# through to not_found_handling) -> /index.html -> ...` and refuse to
# deploy ("Invalid _redirects configuration ... infinite loop").
#
# Fix: rely on wrangler.jsonc's native not_found_handling for SPA fallback
# instead of duplicating it here. Do NOT re-add a `/* ... 200` catch-all
# to this file while that setting is present in wrangler.jsonc.
